> isRef(dict.get("IRT")) ? dict.getRaw("IRT").toString() : null

That won't work at all since `dict.get` dereferences `Ref` objects, whereas `dict.getRaw` doesn't as its name suggests.
```javascript
const rawIRT = dict.getRaw('IRT');
this.data.inReplyTo = isRef(rawIRT) ? rawIRT.toString() : null;
```
